Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): keep recovery guidance and legacy admission
 model-neutral [daveey]

The recovery producer still asked descendants to preserve mandatory concrete pins. Keep acceptance, author exclusions, dependency and subscription gates while emitting class/capability guidance. Exercise both bounded resumes with neutral descendants and unchanged legacy source evidence. Preserve original overlap cases through explicit neutral replay plus historical-pin ingress no-write refusal, and retain actual legacy launch/PID/dry-run assertions without rewriting history. Focused canonical receipts: goal12/0, overlap49/0, refused5/0 and requester consumers9/0, retries disabled; scripts/check21 green. Not broad/CI/live proof; original fleet remediation acceptance remains open.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_resume_requester.py         |  7 +-
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_goal_recovery.py | 11 ++-
 .../test_kanban_refused_pin_clear.py          | 95 ++++++++-----------
 .../tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_roles.py | 32 ++++++-
 4 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 65 deletions(-)

